<p>You have spent time and money getting someone onto your email list. They downloaded your lead magnet, filled out your form, or signed up through your website. Now what? If your answer is "send them a newsletter whenever I remember," you are leaving money on the table.</p>

<p>A drip campaign fixes that problem. It is a pre-written sequence of emails that sends automatically based on a trigger, like signing up, making a purchase, or clicking a link. You build it once. It runs forever. Every new subscriber gets the same carefully crafted experience, whether you are at your desk or on holiday.</p>

<p>The difference between a business that nurtures leads and one that loses them usually comes down to this: did someone follow up, or did the lead go cold? Drip campaigns make sure you always follow up, on time, every time. If you are already exploring <a href="/blog/marketing-automation-getting-started">marketing automation for your business</a>, a drip campaign is one of the highest-impact things you can build.</p>

